.TITLE "diskutil"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages local disks and volumes. It allows you to repair, verify, erase, and partition storage devices directly from the command line.

.DIV "TLDR"
**diskutil list**
Lists all currently available disks and their partitions.
> __list__ display command

**diskutil info device**
Displays detailed information about a specific disk or partition.
> __info__ information command | __device__ the disk identifier

**diskutil mount device**
Mounts a specific volume to the filesystem.
> __mount__ mount command | __device__ the disk identifier

**diskutil unmount device**
Unmounts a specific volume from the filesystem.
> __unmount__ unmount command | __device__ the disk identifier

**diskutil eraseDisk format name device**
Erases a disk and initializes it with a specific format and name.
> __eraseDisk__ formatting command | __format__ filesystem type | __name__ new volume name | __device__ target disk

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always verify the disk identifier using __diskutil list__ before performing destructive operations like __eraseDisk__. Misidentifying a disk can lead to permanent data loss.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:df** **linux:mount**

